MULTI-LICENSE NOTICE
====================

This research-reproduction package uses the following approved license matrix.

1. Software code — MIT License

   The MIT License applies to executable source code and software-support files,
   including Python, shell, and R programs; environment specifications; tests;
   and program configuration files. See LICENSES/MIT.txt.

2. Documents and data — CC BY 4.0

   The Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license applies to the
   authors' original non-code materials, including documentation, manuscript and
   thesis files, figures, panels, legends, tables, provenance records, masks,
   source data, and raw/acquisition-derived data. See
   LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.

A more specific license or attribution notice attached to a file takes
precedence for that file. Third-party materials are not relicensed by this
notice and remain subject to their applicable terms.

Because the software/core Zenodo record contains both categories, its Zenodo
metadata uses the controlled license identifier "other-open" and points to this
matrix. The main-figure, supplementary-figure, and Figure S3 full-resolution
WSI data records use "cc-by-4.0".

Copyright in each work remains with its respective author or copyright holder.
